course: dictionary
lesson: 13603
title: Increased: getting bigger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a number, amount or price goes up, we say it increased. Increased means made bigger or became more. «The price of bread increased last winter.» The bread cost more after the change, so the price went up.
explain: Look at the words after increased to find the clue. «The score increased by 5» means 5 was added. «The score increased to 20» means 20 is the new amount. «Increased from … to» shows both the start and the end.
explain: Increased can also describe a thing. An increased amount is a bigger one than before, so «an increased amount of water» means more water than usual. Check your meaning: if you swap in grew bigger and the sentence still makes sense, you are right.
fact: Increased means made bigger or became more.
fact: Increased is a verb (increase, increases, increasing) and it can also be an adjective.
fact: «Increased by 5» means that 5 was added.
fact: «Increased to 20» means that the new amount is 20.
fact: In science, «the temperature increased as we heated the water» means the water got hotter.
exercise: «The number of pupils increased this year.» What does increased mean here? | Was lost | Became smaller | Stayed the same | *Became more
exercise: «The score increased by 5, from 10 to 15.» How much was added to the score? | 20 | 15 | 10 | *5
exercise: «The temperature increased as we heated the water.» What happened to the temperature? | It froze | It went down | It stayed cold | *It went up
test: «The price increased to 3 pounds.» What is the new price? | 1 pound | *3 pounds | Nothing | 30 pounds
test: Which phrase shows both the start and the end of a change? | increased by | a smaller one | *increased from … to | a bigger one
exam: «An increased amount of water filled the bath.» What does an increased amount mean? | A cold amount | A smaller amount | *A bigger amount than before | No amount at all
